('157', '85', '78', 'THARIN', 'NIMSARA ATTAPATTU', 'Tharinnimsara3@gmail.com', '+94 778 716 205', '0 years', '0 years', 'Pearson BTEC HND in Cyber Security', '30000', 'cv_85_1791947724_6acef3ccd9a8b.pdf', 'THARIN NIMSARA ATTAPATTU\nCyber Security Graduate | SOC / Cyber Security Analyst Trainee\n+94 778 716 205 | Tharinnimsara3@gmail.com | LinkedIn - Tharin Nimsara | Piliyandala, Sri Lanka\n\nPROFESSIONAL SUMMARY\nMotivated Cyber Security graduate with a Pearson BTEC HND in Cyber Security and practical hands-on experience in network security, vulnerability assessment, security monitoring, and IT infrastructure. Skilled in using Wazuh SIEM, Sysmon, pfSense, Tenable Nessus, and Nmap, with practical experience configuring Windows Server Active Directory, DHCP, DNS, Group Policy, and network segmentation. Strong analytical and troubleshooting abilities, including experience leading academic cybersecurity projects, coordinating technical tasks, and working effectively in team environments. Currently progressing toward a BSc(Hons) in Cyber Security and seeking an entry-level Cyber Security Analyst, SOC Analyst, IT Security, or Cyber Security Trainee position where I can apply my technical knowledge, develop industry experience, and contribute to effective security operations.\n\nEDUCATION & QUALIFICATIONS\nBSc (Hons) in Cyber Security (Top Up Degree) | Upcoming / Progression\nPearson BTEC HND in Cyber Security | ESoft Metro Campus / ESU, Colombo 04 | Graduation: August 2026\nPearson Diploma in Information and Communication Technology | ESoft Metro Campus\nPearson Diploma in English\nG.C.E. Ordinary Level (O/L) | 7 Distinctions (A) and 2 Credits (B)\nCore Modules: Network Security, Information Security Management, Cryptography, Ethical Hacking Fundamentals, Computer Systems Architecture.\n\nCYBER SECURITY PROJECTS & PRACTICAL EXPERIENCE\nCorporate Network Deployment - Designed and deployed a secure virtualized corporate network environment using Windows Server Active Directory; configured user accounts, Group Policy Objects (GPOs), DHCP, and DNS.\nSecurity Monitoring - Deployed a centralized Wazuh SIEM pipeline and Sysmon on endpoints to monitor telemetry, analyze event logs, track operational health, and detect simulated brute force incidents.\nVulnerability & Network Assessment - Implemented multi-zone network segmentation using a virtual pfSense Firewall and conducted vulnerability discovery scans with Tenable Nessus and Nmap to identify network risks.\nAcademic Team Project Lead - Coordinated multidisciplinary student teams, delegated responsibilities based on team strengths, managed project timelines, and delivered technical documentation, network topology designs, and security assessments under strict deadlines.\n\nTECHNICAL & PROFESSIONAL SKILLS\nCyber Security: Network Security, Information Assurance, Vulnerability Concepts, Security Monitoring, IT Troubleshooting\nNetworking: Basic Networking, DHCP, DNS, Active Directory, Network Segmentation\nSecurity Tools: Wazuh, Sysmon, pfSense, Tenable Nessus, Nmap\nSystems: Windows / Linux Operating Basics, Virtualized Environments\nSoftware: Microsoft Office Suite, Advanced Excel\nProfessional: Problem Solving, Teamwork, Task Coordination, Time Management, Accountable Decision Making\n\nLANGUAGES & INTERESTS\nLanguages: English (Fluent, Professional Proficiency), Sinhala (Native)\nInterests: Emerging Cyber Threat Landscapes, Continuous Skill Development, Systems Architecture\n\nREFERENCES\nAvailable upon request. Academic or professional references can be furnished promptly to suit employer requirements.', 'extracted', '2026-10-14 03:15:31', '{\"ai_match_score\":78,\"ai_match_reason\":\"The candidate has a Pearson BTEC HND in Cyber Security and relevant academic projects covering network administration, Windows Server Active Directory, and basic infrastructure setup, which align well with the entry-level Trainee IT Associate position. Their stated salary expectation of LKR 30,000 match