('165', '85', '65', 'SARAWANAMUTHU', 'RAJAKULENDREN', 'rajakulendren94@gmail.com', '+94 779144110', '1-2 years', '1-2 years', 'Diploma in English', '30000', 'cv_85_1791948323_6acef6231d496.pdf', 'rajakulentren94@gmail.com | +94 779144110 | No 358 Subo Tarama mw, MipiWigoTa H OelaniXa | DOB: 2001.03.13\nSARAWANAMUTHU RAJAKULYNURYN\n\nPROFILE\nA dedicated and detail-oriented Networking Professional CCNA Certified with strong knowledge in LAN/WAN technologies routing, switching and network troubleshooting. Skilled in configuring Cisco routers and switches implementing VLANs ACLs and routing protocols. Passionate about delivering secure, reliable, and scalable network solutions.\n\nSKILLS & ABILITIES\n• Routing & Switching, VLANs, STP, EtherChannel, Inter-VLAN Routing, NAT, PAT\n• Protocols: TCP/IP, OSPF, EIGRP, RIP, IPv4, IPv6\n• Security: ACLs, VPN basics, Port Security\n• Tools & Simulators: Cisco Packet Tracer, GNS3, Wireshark\n• Systems: Windows Server, Linux (basic administration)\n• Other: Network Troubleshooting, Documentation\n\nEXPERIENCE & PROJECTS\n• Configured and managed Cisco routers and switches in lab simulations\n• Designed and implemented LAN/WAN networks with VLANs and Inter-VLAN routing\n• Applied ACLs (Access Control Lists) to filter and secure network traffic\n• Deployed Routing Protocols (OSPF, EIGRP, RIP) for dynamic routing\n• Configured NAT, PAT and DHCP services for IP management\n• Used Packet Tracer & GNS3 for hands-on troubleshooting and network design\n• Practiced IPv4 and IPv6 addressing with subnetting and supernetting\n• Simulated real-world scenarios such as branch connectivity failover and basic WAN setup\n\nCERTIFICATIONS\n• Cisco Certified Network Associate (CCNA)\n• Diploma in English in Oxford College (Successfully completed Diploma in English lower level through Distinction pass)\n\neducation\n• B/Saraswathy Central College (Political, English, General knowledge)\n• B/Saraswathy Central College (Mathematics, Tamil, Sinhala, Religion, Science, History, ICT, Arts)\n\nLANGUAGES\n• Tamil, Sinhala, English\n\nINTERESTS\n• Team sporting, Reading & writing, Photography, Singing\n\nREFERENCE\n• K Thirulogashankar (Principal, Saraswathy Central College Badulla)\n• R Palanimuthu (Labor Court Lawyer Badulla)', 'extracted', '2026-10-14 03:25:29', '{\"ai_match_score\":65,\"ai_match_reason\":\"The candidate has a solid foundational networking background with CCNA certification and practical lab exposure to LAN\\/WAN technologies, which aligns well with the technical expectations for a Trainee IT Associate. However, the CV lacks explicit evidence of hands-on desktop support, hardware troubleshooting, or end-user interaction. The salary expectation fits well within the company budget.\",\"is_job_mismatch\":false,\"mismatch_reason\":\"\",\"ai_score_breakdown\":{\"skills_match_score\":60,\"experience_match_score\":60,\"qualification_match_score\":75,\"job_description_match_score\":60,\"salary_match_score\":100},\"first_name\":\"SARAWANAMUTHU\",\"last_name\":\"RAJAKULYNURYN\",\"email\":\"rajakulentren94@gmail.com\",\"contact_number\":\"+94779144110\",\"qualification\":\"Diploma in English\",\"overall_experience\":\"1-2 years\",\"relevant_experience\":\"1-2 years\",\"salary_expectation\":\"LKR 30,000\",\"profile_summary\":\"A dedicated and detail-oriented Networking Professional CCNA Certified with strong knowledge in LAN\\/WAN technologies, routing, switching, and network troubleshooting. Skilled in configuring Cisco routers and switches, implementing VLANs, ACLs, and routing protocols. Passionate about delivering secure, reliable, and scalable network solutions.\",\"experience_summary\":\"Hands-on lab simulations configuring and managing Cisco routers and switches, designing LAN\\/WAN networks with VLANs, implementing ACLs, and deploying routing protocols such as OSPF, EIGRP, and RIP.\",\"recruiter_insights\":[\"Candidate holds a CCNA certification and strong networking knowledge, which covers the infrastru