('187', '85', '79', 'Yasiru Udana', 'Kahandagamage', 'yasiruudana1999@gmail.com', '076 071 2656', '0 years', '0 years', 'BEng (Hons) Software Engineering — Staffordshire University', '30000', 'cv_85_1791972898_6acf562248a3b.pdf', 'Yasiru Udana Kahandagamage\nIT Support & Help Desk Specialist\nyasiruudana1999@gmail.com · 076 071 2656 · github.com/yasiru2077 · linkedin.com/in/yasiruudanakahandagamage\n\nPROFESSIONAL SUMMARY\nTechnical support professional transitioning into IT Support / Help Desk roles, combining hands-on Active Directory, DNS, and Group Policy experience from a self-built Windows Server domain lab with a software engineering background in diagnosing, debugging, and resolving system and client-facing issues. Comfortable working directly with end users, ticketing workflows, and cross-functional teams to restore service quickly.\n\nTECHNICAL SKILLS\nIdentity & Access Management: Active Directory, ADUC, User/Group/OU Administration, Password Reset & Account Unlock, Group Policy (GPO)\nNetworking Fundamentals: DNS, DHCP, Static IP Configuration, ipconfig, ping, nslookup, tracert\nWindows Endpoint Support: Windows 10/11 Troubleshooting, Printer & Peripheral Setup, Device Manager/Driver Issues, Microsoft 365 & Outlook\nService Desk & Tools: Ticket Logging & Escalation, Remote Desktop (RDP), VMware Workstation, MySQL, Odoo ERP\nProject Management Tools / Ticketing Systems: Plane, Trello, Zendesk\nSystems & Infrastructure: Docker, Azure, Cloudflare, PostgreSQL, MySQL, MongoDB, Redis, Git\nProgramming Background: JavaScript, TypeScript, Go, Java, Python, SQL\n\nPROJECT — ACTIVE DIRECTORY HOME LAB\nNew Employee Onboarding Simulation (https://github.com/yasiru2077/Enterprise-Windows-Domain-Lab)\n• Built and administered a Windows Server 2022 Active Directory domain from scratch in VMware, including OU structure, user/group provisioning, and GPO-enforced password and lockout policy.\n• Diagnosed and resolved a Group Policy precedence conflict that silently disabled account lockout enforcement, verifying root cause via gpresult and secpol.msc.\n• Joined a Windows 11 client to the domain and deployed a mapped network drive and shared printer via Group Policy, end to end.\n• Simulated and resolved a helpdesk ticket: triggered an account lockout, diagnosed and verified it in Active Directory Users and Computers, reset the password, and restored user access.\n\nEXPERIENCE\nTrainee Full-Stack Developer — Sanmark Solutions\nJul 2025 – Jan 2026\n• Diagnosed and resolved technical issues across applications, servers, and databases, keeping systems stable and minimizing downtime for end users.\n• Provided direct technical support to clients during enterprise ERP (Odoo) implementations, translating business needs into working fixes and configurations.\n• Maintained backend systems integrated with MySQL, troubleshooting data and integration issues to keep production environments running smoothly.\n• Worked cross-functionally with other teams to identify root causes of system issues and resolve them quickly.\n\nIntern Full-Stack Developer — Hotels Hippo\nDec 2023 – Jun 2024\n• Tested and debugged software components, catching and resolving functional issues before they reached users.\n• Maintained system reliability while consistently meeting release deadlines.\n• Resolved user-facing issues based on direct testing and troubleshooting.\n\nEDUCATION\nBEng (Hons) Software Engineering — Staffordshire University, 2022 – 2025\nFCIT — Curtin University, 2020 – 2021\nGCE O/L & A/L — Mahinda College, 2005 – 2018', 'extracted', '2026-10-14 16:09:04', '{\"ai_match_score\":79,\"ai_match_reason\":\"Yasiru presents a solid educational background with a BEng (Hons) in Software Engineering, exceeding the baseline diploma requirement, alongside hands-on home lab experience with Windows Server, Active Directory, and networking fundamentals. However, the CV lacks explicit mention of a valid motorbike license and direct hardware troubleshooting\\/repair e