unts, printers, and local network issues.\n- Recorded incidents, tracked resolutions, and prepared simple user guides for recurring support requests.\n- Assisted with workstation setup, software installation, and routine system checks.\n\nEDUCATION & QUALIFICATIONS\nBSc (Hons) in Software Engineering | Sample Institute of Technology | 2023 - 2026 | Sri Lanka\n- Key areas: Software Engineering, Web Development, Databases, Computer Networks, Software Testing, Project Management.\n- Final-year project: Web-based Recruitment Management System with candidate tracking and role-based access control.\n\nG.C.E. Advanced Level - Commerce Stream | Sample Central College | 2022\nG.C.E. Ordinary Level | Sample Central College | 2019\n\nSELECTED PROJECTS\nRecruitment Management System | Academic Project | 2026\n- Developed a role-based recruitment system for administrators, HR users, and applicants.\n- Implemented vacancy management, applicant records, interview tracking, and status updates.\n- Technologies: React.js, PHP, MySQL, HTML5, CSS3, REST-style API integration.\n\nPersonal Task & Expense Tracker | Personal Project | 2025\n- Built a responsive dashboard to manage tasks, categories, expenses, and monthly summaries.\n- Added form validation, reusable UI components, filtering, and persistent database storage.\n\nCERTIFICATIONS & TRAINING\n- Introduction to Web Development - Sample Online Academy, 2025\n- Git & GitHub Fundamentals - Sample Learning Platform, 2025\n- SQL Basics and Database Design - Sample Learning Platform, 2024\n- Workplace Communication and Professional Skills - Sample Training Centre, 2024\n\nTECHNICAL KNOWLEDGE\n- Object-oriented programming concepts, client-server architecture, CRUD operations, and REST API fundamentals.\n- Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC), requirements gathering, use cases, UML basics, and Agile/Scrum concepts.\n- Functional testing, test-case preparation, defect reporting, input validation, and basic security awareness.\n- Databa