('205', '89', '78', 'GeorgeSteuart', 'Doe', 'Doe@gmail.com', '+94771234567', '1-2 years', '1-2 years', 'BSc (Hons) in Software Engineering', '120000', 'cv_89_1792382149_6ad594c552d6e.pdf', 'NADUMI PERERA\nSoftware Engineering Graduate | Junior Full-Stack Developer\nnadumi672@gmail.com\n+94 77 123 4567\nColombo, Sri Lanka\nlinkedin.com/in/nadumi-perera\ngithub.com/nadumi-perera\n\nPROFESSIONAL SUMMARY\nMotivated Software Engineering graduate with hands-on experience in web application development, database design, API integration, testing, and collaborative software projects. Comfortable working with React, JavaScript, PHP, MySQL, Git, and modern development workflows. Strong problem-solving, communication, and documentation skills, with a keen interest in building secure and user-friendly systems.\n\nCORE SKILLS\nFrontend: React.js, JavaScript, HTML5, CSS3, Responsive UI\nBackend: PHP, REST APIs, Node.js fundamentals\nDatabase: MySQL, SQL queries, relational database design\nTools & Practices: Git, GitHub, VS Code, Postman, Agile/Scrum, QA testing, documentation\nOther: Microsoft Office, Figma basics, troubleshooting\nSoft Skills: Teamwork, communication, time management, analytical thinking\nLanguages: English, Sinhala\nAvailability: Open to junior software engineering / IT roles\n\nWORK EXPERIENCE\nJunior Software Developer Intern | Nova Digital Solutions (Sample Company) | Jan 2026 - Jun 2026\n- Supported the development and maintenance of responsive web applications using React, JavaScript, HTML, and CSS.\n- Integrated frontend forms with backend APIs and validated data before database submission.\n- Created and tested MySQL queries for application modules, reports, and basic data validation.\n- Used Git and GitHub for version control, branch-based development, code reviews, and issue tracking.\n- Assisted with functional testing, bug fixing, documentation, and deployment checks.\n\nIT Support Trainee | Bluewave Business Services (Sample Company) | Aug 2025 - Dec 2025 | Kandy, Sri Lanka\n- Provided first-line support for desktop software, user accounts, printers, and local network issues.\n- Recorded incidents, tracked resolutions, and prepared simple user guides for recurring support requests.\n- Assisted with workstation setup, software installation, and routine system checks.\n\nEDUCATION & QUALIFICATIONS\nBSc (Hons) in Software Engineering | Sample Institute of Technology | 2023 - 2026 | Sri Lanka\n- Key areas: Software Engineering, Web Development, Databases, Computer Networks, Software Testing, Project Management.\n- Final-year project: Web-based Recruitment Management System with candidate tracking and role-based access control.\n\nG.C.E. Advanced Level - Commerce Stream | Sample Central College | 2022\n- Completed Advanced Level examination with subjects including Accounting, Business Studies, and Economics.\n\nG.C.E. Ordinary Level | Sample Central College | 2019\n- Completed Ordinary Level examination including English, Mathematics, Science, ICT, and Sinhala.\n\nSELECTED PROJECTS\nRecruitment Management System | Academic Project | 2026\n- Developed a role-based recruitment system for administrators, HR users, and applicants.\n- Implemented vacancy management, applicant records, interview tracking, and status updates.\n- Technologies: React.js, PHP, MySQL, HTML5, CSS3, REST-style API integration.\n\nPersonal Task & Expense Tracker | Personal Project | 2025\n- Built a responsive dashboard to manage tasks, categories, expenses, and monthly summaries.\n- Added form validation, reusable UI components, filtering, and persistent database storage.\n\nCERTIFICATIONS & TRAINING\n- Introduction to Web Development - Sample Online Academy, 2025\n- Git & GitHub Fundamentals - Sample Learning Platform, 2025\n- SQL Basics and Database Design - Sample Learning Platform, 2024\n- Workplace Communication and Professional Skills - Sample Training Centre, 2024\n\nADDITIONAL INFORMATION\nNationality: Sri Lankan\nLanguages: Sinhala - Native | English - Professional working proficiency\nInterests: Web development, UI/UX, software testing, technology learning\n\nTECHNICAL KNOWLEDGE\n- Object-oriented programming concepts, client-server architecture, CRUD operations, and REST API fundamentals.\n- Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC), requirements gathering, use cases, UML basics, and Agile/Scrum concepts.\n- Functional testing, test-case preparation, defect reporting, input validation, and basic security awareness.\n- Database normalization, joins, filtering, aggregation, constraints, and basic query optimization concepts.\n\nACHIEVEMENTS & LEADERSHIP\n- Completed multiple university group software projects and contributed to requirements, UI implementation, testing, and documentation.\n- Presented academic project demonstrations to lecturers and peers, explaining system workflows and technical decisions.\n- Supported classmates with Git/GitHub workflows and basic frontend debugging during collaborative assignments.\n\nVOLUNTEER & EXTRA-CURRICULAR ACTIVITIES\n- Volunteer - University Technology Society: assisted with event coordination, registration, and technical setup.\n- Participated in student workshops on career readiness, teamwork, presentation skills, and professional communication.\n\nREFERENCES\nMs. Anjali Fernando | Senior Lecturer, Sample Institute of Technology | Email: anjali.fernando@example.com | Phone: +94 71 555 0101\nMr. Kavindu Silva | Software Engineering Lead, Nova Digital Solutions | Email: kavindu.silva@example.com | Phone: +94 76 555 0202', 'extracted', '2026-10-19 03:55:55', '{\"ai_match_score\":78,\"ai_match_reason\":\"Nadumi Perera presents a solid foundation with a BSc (Hons) in Software Engineering and foundational exposure to QA testing, functional testing, and bug fixing during her internship. While her primary focus is full-stack development, her academic background in software testing and QA exposure aligns reasonably well with a Junior QA position, though her salar