('206', '89', '19', 'Kasuni', 'Perera', 'samadhi@gsoptimize.lk', '+94 77 482 3165', '3-4 years', '0 years', 'Bachelor of Business Management (Hons) in Human Resource Management', '100000', 'cv_89_1792383071_6ad5985feaa1d.pdf', 'Kavindi Senanayake\nHR Executive | Recruitment | HR Administration | Employee Relations\nColombo, Sri Lanka | +94 77 482 3165 | kavindi.senanayake@example.com | linkedin.com/in/kavindisenanayake\n\nPROFESSIONAL SUMMARY\nProactive and detail-oriented HR Executive with over 3 years of experience in recruitment, onboarding, employee records, attendance and leave administration, HR documentation, performance support, employee engagement, and HR reporting. Experienced in coordinating full-cycle recruitment activities, maintaining confidential employee data, preparing HR letters and reports, and supporting managers with day-to-day people operations. Proficient in Microsoft Excel, Microsoft 365, HRIS platforms, and candidate tracking systems. Strong communication, organization, confidentiality, and interpersonal skills with a practical understanding of Sri Lankan HR practices.\n\nCORE HR SKILLS\nRecruitment & Selection: Job posting, CV screening, candidate shortlisting, interview scheduling, offer coordination\nHR Administration: Employee files, HR letters, contracts, confirmation documentation, record maintenance\nEmployee Lifecycle: Onboarding, orientation, probation tracking, transfers, resignations, exit clearance\nAttendance & Leave: Attendance monitoring, leave records, monthly summaries, employee follow-up\nPerformance & Training: Appraisal coordination, training schedules, development records, evaluation support\nEmployee Relations: Employee queries, engagement activities, communication, issue escalation\nHR Systems & Tools: HRIS, applicant tracking systems, Microsoft Excel, Word, PowerPoint, Microsoft 365\nReporting: Headcount reports, recruitment status reports, attendance reports, HR dashboards\n\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE\nHR Executive\nApex Business Solutions (Pvt) Ltd - Colombo, Sri Lanka | Apr 2024 - Present\n- Coordinate end-to-end recruitment activities for executive, administrative, technical, and support roles.\n- Publish job vacancies, screen CVs, prepare candidate shortlists, schedule interviews, and communicate with applicants.\n- Prepare appointment letters, confirmation letters, service letters, transfer letters, and other employee documentation.\n- Maintain employee personal files, HRIS records, emergency contact details, and confidential personnel information.\n- Manage attendance and leave records and prepare monthly summaries for payroll and management review.\n- Coordinate new employee onboarding, orientation sessions, policy briefings, and probation follow-up activities.\n- Support performance appraisal cycles by preparing schedules, forms, reminders, and completion reports.\n- Assist with employee engagement activities, staff events, training programs, and internal communication initiatives.\n- Prepare monthly HR reports covering headcount, recruitment status, staff turnover, attendance, leave, and vacancies.\n- Support resignation, clearance, exit interview, and final documentation processes.\n- Respond to routine employee HR queries and escalate sensitive matters to the HR Manager when required.\n- Maintain high standards of confidentiality when handling employee and management information.\n\nHR Assistant\nCeylon Corporate Services (Pvt) Ltd - Colombo, Sri Lanka | Jan 2023 - Mar 2024\n- Assisted with recruitment advertisements, CV screening, interview coordination, and candidate database updates.\n- Prepared onboarding checklists, employee files, ID requests, and orientation documents for new employees.\n- Updated attendance, leave, probation, and employee master records using the company HR system.\n- Supported payroll preparation by checking attendance, no-pay leave, overtime, and employee changes.\n- Maintained training attendance records and assisted with staff development programs.\n- Helped organize employee engagement events, staff welfare activities, and internal meetings.\n- Prepared basic HR reports using Microsoft Excel, including leave summaries, headcount data, and recruitment trackers.\n- Filed HR documents systematically and assisted during internal and external HR audits.\n\nHR Intern\nLanka Consumer Products PLC - Wattala, Sri Lanka | Jul 2022 - Dec 2022\n- Supported the HR team with filing, data entry, recruitment coordination, and employee record updates.\n- Assisted with interview scheduling and candidate communication.\n- Prepared employee documentation and maintained training and attendance records.\n- Participated in induction sessions and staff engagement activities.\n\nEDUCATION\nBachelor of Business Management (Hons) in Human Resource Management\nMetropolitan University of Sri Lanka | 2018 - 2022\nRelevant modules: Human Resource Management, Recruitment and Selection, Employee Relations, Performance Management, Training and Development, Organizational Behaviour, Business Law, Strategic Management, and Research Methods.\n\nProfessional Qualification in Human Resource Management\nInstitute of Personnel Management - Sri Lanka | 2022\n\nCERTIFICATIONS & TRAINING\n- Advanced Microsoft Excel for HR Professionals - 2025\n- Certificate in Labour Law and Employee Relations - 2024\n- Interviewing and Candidate Selection Workshop - 2024\n- HR Analytics Fundamentals - 2023\n- Microsoft 365 Productivity Training - 2023\n\nKEY ACHIEVEMENTS\n- Improved recruitment tracking by introducing a structured candidate status tracker used by the HR team.\n- Supported the successful onboarding of more than 60 employees across multiple departments.\n- Helped reduce delays in monthly attendance reporting by standardizing the HR attendance review process.\n- Coordinated employee engagement activities with participation from staff across multiple business units.\n\nHR SYSTEMS & SOFTWARE\nMicrosoft Excel | Microsoft Word | Microsoft PowerPoint